WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.230
Here is a tiny triangle, small
enough to fit on a stamp.

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.470
Here is a giant triangle,
as big as a football pitch.

3
00:00:08.520 --> 00:00:12.230
Measure the three angles inside
each one, and add them up.

4
00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:15.190
The giant triangle is so much bigger.

5
00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:17.730
So will its angles add up to more?

6
00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.950
Or could the totals be the same?

7
00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.570
In this mission, you'll learn
angle facts for a straight line,

8
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.130
for a point, and for a triangle.

9
00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.950
Then you'll find the total of
the angles inside any polygon,

10
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.150
like a pentagon or a hexagon.

11
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:36.510
Your mission: compare the angle
totals of the two triangles.
